    "title": "Speaking and interaction practice",
    "subtitle": "A missing item in the returned bag",
    "context": "The reader reconstructs the item’s location and rejects the mistaken accusation. Express this outcome using the unit’s selected vocabulary and constructions.",
    "steps": [
      {
        "id": "EX-CORE-U5-43-required-interaction-produce",
        "kind": "check",
        "title": "Respond to the situation",
        "questions": [
          {
            "id": "EX-CORE-U5-43-required-interaction-draft",
            "kind": "production",
            "response": "spoken",
            "prompt": "A missing item in the returned bag: A partner favors a different response to this situation. Ask which source detail supports their view, acknowledge the relevant point, and explain your response without overstating the evidence.",
            "promptLanguage": "en",
            "context": "朋友把一个袋子忘在活动房间，回来寻找时，工作人员把袋子还给了他。他打开一看，发现里面少了一张重要的卡，马上担心有人拿走了。\n\n工作人员请他先想一想出门前怎么放的。他说自己把袋子系好，还检查过结，可是怕重要的卡丢了，没有直接和其他东西放在一起。\n\n说到这里，他想起来，自己把卡藏在外套里面的口袋里。后来天热，他脱下外套交给另一位朋友，离开时只记得拿袋子，却忘了外套。\n\n我们联系了保管外套的朋友，他果然在外套口袋里找到了那张卡。袋子里没有卡，不是因为工作人员把它弄丢了，而是因为卡一直放在外套里。\n\n朋友知道自己误会了工作人员，就认真向对方道歉。他把卡放回自己记得的地方，又把外套和袋子一起拿好，不再把它们分开放。\n\n离开前，他又摸了摸口袋，笑着把刚才的担心告诉我。这次终于可以放心走了，袋子上的结还在，卡也找到了，工作人员不用再继续帮忙查找。",
            "contextLanguage": "zh",
            "label": "Take your speaking turn",
            "resultDomain": "Self-reviewed speaking practice",
            "rubric": [
              {
                "id": "r1",
                "text": "My clarification targets the partner’s reason."
              },
              {
                "id": "r2",
                "text": "My response addresses that reason and preserves the source’s limits."
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "sequential": true
      }
